# Decision — canonical LAB console topology B+D revision2

## Exact owner approval and integral review

Owner explicitly approved ONLY revision2 R0–R7 in OWNER APPROVAL — B+D REVISION2, NORMATIVE ONLY. Approved candidate SHA256 3c1230cab06b4a38952976a590321583c1c256eebd01ff8ee759f9913f420086. The exact source bytes were independently verified before this record; [integral clause review](../integration/canonical-lab-console-topology-bd-20261023/integral-review.md) and [acceptance verification](../integration/canonical-lab-console-topology-bd-20261023/acceptance-verification.json) govern this documentary registration. The approved write and byte-exact post-write verification complete normative registration, not implementation qualification. No external reviewer or runtime proof is invented by this record.

[Candidate revision2](ADR-CANDIDATE-canonical-lab-console-census-resolution-20261023.md) and its [approved byte-exact archive](../integration/canonical-lab-console-topology-bd-20261023/approved-revision2-original.md) remain historically PROPOSED and unchanged; acceptance is recorded HERE. Revision1 [original archive](../integration/canonical-lab-console-topology-bd-20261023/proposal-revision1-original.md) remains byte-exact, SHA256 d8db1a16fbfa5ec6fd4984d1d5a7fc6a6db70eafc3c1012cb15d08a8d70d1dac. Its relationship/identity uncertainty waiver was rejected and is NOT accepted.

## Normative composition and independent gates

This is a focal amendment of the SAME [accepted ED11 single-LAB B0–B6 decision](DECISION-ed11-single-lab-diagnostic-native-boundary-20261023.md), whose original bytes remain unchanged, SHA256 e7031bd29c9bd174359ffcc3c9a021a6ad25a0256a5cf03b40c0866d3a5776b7. Within the exact named LAB scope, R1/R4 specialize B4.B.4 topology/accounting to one already-elevated PowerShell, native qualifier, future LAB service and at most one factually proved console infrastructure process: four actual processes/papéis maximum, no fifth slot. R2/R3 specialize mandatory console evidence, without waiving B4.D security; R5/R6 preserve authority, exclusivity, confirmation, one-shot consumption, Stop and retained lifetime. Topology/policy revision binding under B4.B.6 must use this amendment after implementation qualification. All unmodified B0–B6 clauses and O0–O5 remain controlling. No general production contract or quota is revised.

The console and PowerShell remain separately enumerated processes with explicit combined administrative accounting. Native qualifier/service EACH retain128-handle guard; no transfer of their costs to evade it. HOST_CREDITS=NONE_GRANTED; no refund, quota increase, hidden console cost or promotion of UNKNOWN. Existing freshness/headroom, smaller controlled quotas, total caps and retained-charge rules remain.

Identity, factual console linkage, provenance, session, lifetime and mandatory observable resources must be PROVED. Missing/unsupported/uncertain relationship => DENY even after approval, elevation or mutex acquisition. Existing106-handle observation, snapshot name/parent, client/window/current-file evidence do not prove any current console satisfies these conditions. No factual console relationship, readiness, quiescence or ED11 operational PASS is declared here.

Prospective phrases such as proposed/future/after acceptance in the preserved R0–R7 body resolve to ACCEPTED NORMATIVE POLICY only through THIS owner record. They never grant implementation or operation authority. Canonical native owner remains sole admission/consumption/Stop/retention authority; infrastructure is never another owner or credential.

IMPLEMENTATION_AUTHORIZED=NO. No source/launcher/census/bin/pin change, preflight, StartService/StopService, SCM rebind, ACL, CA, certificates, bootstrap, CURRENT, new trace or handle measurement is authorized. A later scoped implementation authorization, qualified proof mechanism, reviewed patch/build/tests, and separate exact manual operation approval are still required. ED11 remains PARTIAL; CURRENT/signature/authoritative recovery remain DENY; production0.6.4/PST/Browser/PACC wire unchanged.

## Accepted R0–R7 — byte-exact revision2 body

The following body SHA256 is 2289ea667cd3ea69e45c6f2161d565c02cf3c4e7c7b3bf3c58861c215ea27b1e (UTF-8 bytes from R0 through R7, excluding surrounding headings/newlines).

R0. Scope remains the exact existing single diagnostic LAB attempt/host/boot/service/candidate/configuration and its consumed-once intent. No new service, owner, registry, provider or general production allowance. The candidate changes topology/administrative binding only after explicit acceptance; it does not amend O0–O5 or retire any historical UNKNOWN.

R1. Replace the two distinct PowerShell administrative actors with ONE already-elevated interactive Windows PowerShell5.1 actor invoking the script inside its existing process (no powershell.exe wrapper and no UAC child). Retain one native qualifier and one future service. Up to ONE explicitly approved Windows console infrastructure process may coexist. Maximum actual operation processes remains FOUR, not five. Absence of console infrastructure leaves capacity unused, never a credit. Existing outside terminal/OS baseline remains measured, not hidden; any operation-related additional process outside this explicit set denies admission.

R2. The fourth role is at most ONE Windows console infrastructure process FACTUALLY LINKED to the authorized attempt. It is neither administrative authority nor an additional application admission. The exact contemporary host/boot/process identity must be included in the same plan and explicit confirmation. Require original native process handle and creation identity, factual console relationship to the elevated actor/attempt, native image identity and provenance, session/token context, live lifetime, observable resources and ED11 accounting. Evidence must remain valid through the required observation/admission interval; failed revalidation invalidates eligibility. Name conhost.exe, textual path, parent PID, same session, owner designation or console client-list membership alone or in an unqualified combination do not establish the required relationship/provenance. Unknown/unrelated/reused/divergent/unapproved instances, missing mandatory evidence or a second infrastructure instance cause DENY. A named current file must not be silently equated to the process mapped image. Enumerate all actual processes in the SAME census; report the exact evidence and limits. No global whitelist, arbitrary-child exemption, automatic adoption of historical PIDs or fifth slot.

R3. There is NO risk-acceptance substitute for the R2 mandatory identity, factual relationship, provenance, session, lifetime and observable resource evidence. If the relationship cannot be proved, DENY, even after normative approval, owner confirmation or successful canonical mutex acquisition. If no supported mechanism sufficient for a required fact has been qualified, retain that implementation/admission gate as unsatisfied; do not invent an authenticated API or turn a diagnostic correlation into authority. Existing ED11 B4.D residual uncertainty remains limited to the already accepted resource/measurement scope (kernel/cache attribution, transitive stack, between-sample peaks and external concurrency). It does not waive native identity/security, required metrics, Stop, quiescence or lifetime. UNKNOWN remains explicit; no conversion to zero or success. Existing historic106 handles and console observations are not proof that this fourth role currently qualifies.

R4. Charge the PowerShell PLUS the one designated infrastructure process as a combined administrative budget observation (two separately enumerated process roles, NEVER one census process): sum Private Bytes/current commit/current Working Set and handles/threads/observable stack respectively, each process observed and attributed separately before summation. Combined guards remain256MiB,1024 handles,64 threads,32MiB observable committed stack VA. Peak observations remain per-process; do not invent a simultaneous sum of unrelated historical peaks. Qualifier/service EACH remain64MiB,128 handles,16 threads,8MiB stack. Thus tighter proposed administrative/native subtotal is384MiB/1280 handles/96 threads/48MiB stack; original overall640MiB/2304/160/80MiB ceilings also remain. These are selected risk guards, not quotas or measured capacities. Never offset a failed individual128 native guard with administrative spare capacity. No credits; unknown native/kernel/cache/stack costs remain explicit and charged/retained according to accepted policy. Existing numeric guards remain in force until this amendment is accepted and implemented.

R5. Elevation does not replace explicit administrative authorization or exact confirmation. Preserve approved operator SID, elevated token, no impersonation, interactive console, exact presented plan and token continuity. Same canonical native owner acquires exclusivity BEFORE census/effects and keeps it through measurement, effect/Stop and UNKNOWN. Reducing administrative actors does not merge roles by passing the same PID twice to current ig_actor. A future revised API must accept one verified launcher handle+creation+SID/token and qualifier identity, bind exact attempt/plan/configuration/candidate/policy revision and explicit confirmation, and reject replay/substitution/token change/duplicate consumption. Existing native confirmation can remain on the inherited console; an infrastructure designation never replaces it. Preserve canonical mutex, intent, read-only/nonconsuming preparation, original first error and all Stop/retirement guards.

R6. Keep console-based operator Stop and canonical Stop semantics for this smaller proposed topology. Absence of a usable confirmation/Stop console denies this topology; do not substitute no-window for authority. Stop-before-confirmation/before-effects aborts; Stop-after-effect enters existing single safe Stop/retention rules. Failed read/close, process loss, ambiguous disposition or non-quiescent dependencies retain UNKNOWN, pins/handles/charges; no kill, retry, automatic rearming or timeout cleanup. A genuinely console-independent topology remains a separate future implementation option requiring its own verified Stop/binding, not an implicit approval here.

R7. Required before implementation activation: explicit normative acceptance, exact patch review of existing launcher/ig_actor/census/observer integration, four warning-free builds, negative/model/process-fixture suite and separate approval for one manual read-only native qualification. Current consumed administrative ED11H-20261023-01 claim is immutable; cannot be reused/rearmed. Exact-operation Start/rebind approval remains separate and absent. No new trace or handle measurement is authorized by acceptance. No productive promotion, CA, issuance, CURRENT or network.

